Upstream source-signing public keys, one armored export per key, named <FINGERPRINT>.asc
(40 uppercase hex, the PRIMARY key). base/sources.lock pins which key must have signed
which source; base/river-build dearmors the one key into a private keyring per check and
never touches a user keyring. Empty today: the three starter sources (skalibs, execline,
s6) are from skarnet.org, which publishes no signatures (see the nosig lines in the lock).

These keys vouch for UPSTREAM bytes only. The key that vouches for what RIVER itself ships
is the owner's, in ../owner/.
